# copytree ignore — gitignore semantics, applied on top of .gitignore.
# Keep the AI context compact by excluding what the Go toolchain generates or
# what carries no semantic value for reading the source. Build output, the
# binary, *.test/*.out, coverage, profiles, .env*, logs and state.db are already
# handled by .gitignore, so they're not repeated here.

# The test suite dominates the tree (~half of all .go files). The Go toolchain
# names every test file `*_test.go`, so this single pattern catches all of them
# wherever they live — no need for a defensive second rule like the TS config had.
*_test.go

# Conventional Go test fixtures — data-only, irrelevant to reading the code.
testdata/

# Vendored dependencies, if ever checked in (`go mod vendor`): third-party
# source we don't author and don't want bloating the context.
vendor/

# Dependency checksums — 12 KiB of opaque hashes with zero semantic value for an
# AI reading the project. go.mod (module path + the dep list) is kept; go.sum is not.
go.sum

# Build-time blank import anchor — explicitly carries no runtime effect; only
# purpose is to prevent `go mod tidy` from removing deps before subsystems use them.
internal/deps/deps.go

# Splash animation data — 24KB of raw block-character (█) frame arrays. Pure data,
# zero semantic value for reading the source or understanding the system.
internal/ui/splash_frames.go

# Boot/splash animation logic — runs once at startup, self-contained visual sugar
# with no architectural bearing on the rest of the codebase.
internal/ui/splash.go
internal/ui/boot_splash.go

# UI theming — colour, font, and glyph constants. Design decisions, not logic;
# not where bugs or architectural choices live.
internal/ui/theme/

# Markdown renderer — thin wrapper around glamour; mechanical implementation detail
# with no bearing on the agent loop, tools, or storage layers.
internal/ui/markdown/

# Runtime recipe config — user-generated/project-specific data, not source code.
.daintree/
